# Byte Run (FLI)

# Each line of the image is compressed separately. For a real FLI file, the
# packets of each line will add up to 320 pixels rendered.  Since each
# packet is limited to a run of 127 pixels, the typical idiom encountered
# is to see 3 packets per line, of size 127, 127, 66.
#
# To exercise our unit test, we want both positive and negative counts.
# So, each line will call for 4 packets.
# Packet 0 is a repeated run of 7F (127) bytes in color 0.
# Packet 1 is a custom   run of FB ( -5) bytes in colors 1 to 5
# Packet 2 is a repeated run of 70 (112) bytes in color 6.
# Packet 2 is a repeated run of 4C ( 76) bytes in color 7.


04 7F00 FB0102030405 7006 4C07 # line 0
